[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 803,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 607,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122643,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 209,
        "headingId": 607,
        "headingText": "<p>Secretory carcinoma (SC) is a salivary gland&ndash;type carcinoma often composed of microcystic, tubular, and solid structures with abundant eosinophilic homogeneous or bubbly secretions. It is usually characterized by specific rearrangement of the <em>ETV6</em>&nbsp;gene.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-12-17T13:10:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 804,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 608,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122644,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 209,
        "headingId": 608,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8502/3 Secretory carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T11:58:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 805,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 609,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122645,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 209,
        "headingId": 609,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2D10.Y &amp; XH44J4 Other specified malignant neoplasms of thyroid gland &amp; Secretory carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T11:58:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 806,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 610,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122646,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 209,
        "headingId": 610,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> mammary analogue secretory carcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T11:58:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 807,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 611,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122647,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 209,
        "headingId": 611,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T11:58:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 808,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 612,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122648,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 209,
        "headingId": 612,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SC can occur in either lobe or in the isthmus.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T11:58:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 809,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 613,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122649,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 209,
        "headingId": 613,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SC usually presents as a uninodular mass. Compression or invasion of adjacent structures and nodal disease are more common than in salivary SC {30564997; 32562215}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T11:58:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 810,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 614,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122650,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 209,
        "headingId": 614,
        "headingText": "<p>Average age at presentation is slightly older than at salivary gland sites (61.5&nbsp;years, range: 36&ndash;74 years). There appears to be a female predilection {30564997; 32562215}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-12-20T13:40:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 811,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 615,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122651,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 209,
        "headingId": 615,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is unclear. Occasional co-occurrence with papillary thyroid carcinoma, including rare cases with shared translocations, is noted {27282352}, implying a possible follicular origin.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T11:58:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 812,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 616,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122652,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 209,
        "headingId": 616,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SCs are characterized by <em>ETV6</em> translocations, with <em>ETV6</em>::<em>NTRK3</em> exclusively seen in the thyroid to date {34655408}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T11:58:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 819,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 623,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122653,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 209,
        "headingId": 623,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The mean size of reported thyroid SCs is 44&nbsp;mm (range: 24&ndash;76&nbsp;mm). They show firm, white-tan, often infiltrative cut surfaces {30564997; 32562215}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T11:58:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 813,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 617,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122654,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 209,
        "headingId": 617,
        "headingText": "<p>Thyroid SCs are morphologically similar to SCs at other sites and are composed of cells with eosinophilic, vacuolated cytoplasm, arranged in papillary, tubular, microcystic, and solid patterns. SC characteristically shows eosinophilic, bubbly luminal secretions. Rare cases show high-grade transformation {28556362; 30564997; 34655408}.</p>\r\n<h6><em>Immunohistochemistry</em></h6>\r\n<p>SCs characteristically stain for S100, mammaglobin, GATA3, and (often) GCDFP-15. Thyroglobulin and thyroid transcription factor&nbsp;1 (TTF1) are typically negative, with weak, focal PAX8 staining {27400918; 32562215}. PAS and mucicarmine usually highlight the secretions.</p>\r\n<h6><em>Differential diagnosis</em></h6>\r\n<p>Architecture, nuclear features, and eosinophilic cytoplasm may raise consideration for oncocytic carcinoma, medullary carcinoma, and papillary thyroid carcinoma. However, the characteristic cytoplasm, secretions, and immunophenotype are highly unlikely to be seen outside of SC. Secondary involvement by a non-thyroid SC should be excluded clinicoradiologically.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T11:58:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 814,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 618,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122655,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 209,
        "headingId": 618,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Aspirates show cohesive vaguely histiocytoid cells with eosinophilic vacuolar cytoplasm arranged in sheets or arborizing 3D structures. Nuclei have moderate size variation and may show clearing, prominent nucleoli, and membrane irregularities such as grooves or rare pseudoinclusions {27633961}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T11:58:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 815,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 619,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122656,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 209,
        "headingId": 619,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>ETV6</em> translocations confirm the diagnosis when present along with the typical morphology and immunophenotype.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T11:58:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 818,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 622,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122657,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 209,
        "headingId": 622,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> eosinophilic vacuolar cells; bubbly secretions; microcystic, tubular, solid, and papillary architecture; S100/SOX10 (not well studied in thyroid SC) and mammaglobin expression; absent to weak thyroid differentiation marker expression.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> <em>ETV6</em> translocation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T11:58:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 816,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 620,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122658,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 209,
        "headingId": 620,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Staging is according to the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) and American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) staging systems.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T11:58:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 817,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 621,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122659,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 209,
        "headingId": 621,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Thyroid SCs appear more aggressive than their salivary counterparts. More than half of patients experience either locoregional recurrence or distant metastases. Positive margins and extrathyroidal extension may be associated with recurrence {30564997; 32562215}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T11:58:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]